>  And to separate the code of generating that data (which at the end produces the container) and the plotter...
I definitely agree here and would want to make sure to maintain this methodology for all of my ideas mentioned above.

> We would really like to "know" though the software whether a learner supports this (eg using mlr's tagging mechansim) and have a common API call for this.

To make sure I'm following, are you referring to the property tags for a given learner? Such as mentioned in https://github.com/mlr-org/mlr/blob/master/R/RLearner.R.

> Dummy models I guess you mean? So the most naive model as a base line?

Exactly. A dummy classifier could do things like mimic the training set's class distribution, predict the most frequent class, among other options.

Do you and the rest of the team have any other ideas on the roadmap that might complement the ideas mentioned so far? Anything I might have left out?

