It would certainly be reasonable to use specific standard error methods
for specific performance or risk metrics, where they exist.

It is probably still important to allow the user to also do some other
model, like a bootstrap or Newey-West

All estimates of standard error have certain assumptions baked in.  It
is important that these be documented, and that the user who believes
one or more of the assumptions has been violated is free to test a
method of calculating standard error that may shed light on the situation.

